id: 13
hanzi: 婚姻
pinyin: hūn yīn
level: HSK 5
part_of_speech: Noun

meanings_summary:
  en: marriage; matrimony; marital relationship
  es: matrimonio; unión conyugal; nupcias

senses[1]{sense_number,part_of_speech,register,definition_en,definition_es,example_phrase}:
  1 | Noun | Standard | the legally or socially recognized union of two people as partners in a personal relationship | unión legal y socialmente reconocida de dos personas como pareja conyugal | 婚姻幸福 (happy marriage)

example_sentences[2]{id,hanzi,pinyin,en,es}:
  #1 | 在长达数十年的婚姻旅程中，相互信任与包容是化解生活琐事争执、保持感情历久弥新的坚实基石。 | Zài chángdá shù shí nián de hūnyīn lǚchéng zhōng, xiānghù xìnrèn yǔ bāoróng shì huàjiě shēnghuó suǒshì zhēngzhí, bǎochí gǎnqíng lìjiǔmíxīn de jiānshí jīshí. | Across a decades-long marital journey, mutual trust and tolerance are the solid cornerstone resolving daily domestic squabbles and keeping affection fresh. | A lo largo de décadas de matrimonio, la confianza y la tolerancia mutuas son la piedra angular para resolver roces diarios y mantener vivo el amor.
  #2 | 社会学学者通过跟踪调查指出，当代青年群体对婚姻制度的认知正从功能性结盟转向精神契合度优先。 | Shèhuìxué xuézhě tōngguò gēnzōng diàochá zhǐchū, dāngdài qīngnián qúntǐ duì hūnyīn zhìdù de rènzhī zhèng cóng gōngnéngxìng jiéméng zhuǎnxiàng jīngshén qìhédù yōuxiān. | Sociologists point out via longitudinal surveys that modern youth's perception of marriage is shifting from functional alliance toward spiritual compatibility. | A través de estudios sociológicos, se observa que los jóvenes conciben el matrimonio no como una alianza utilitaria, sino como una afinidad espiritual prioritaria.

