  千里姻缘 | qiān lǐ yīn yuán | romantic affinity bringing people together from a thousand miles apart
  秦晋之好 | qín jìn zhī hǎo | match between two families; firm matrimonial alliance
  结为连理 | jié wéi lián lǐ | join together as intertwining branches; tie the knot

character_decomposition[2]{character,pinyin,meaning_en,meaning_es,radical,radical_meaning_en,meaning_component,sound_component,stroke_count,composition_type,etymology_and_mnemonic,visual_mnemonic_story_en,visual_mnemonic_story_es,tone_mnemonic_anchor,cangjie,traditional}:
  婚 | hūn | marry; wedding; bridegroom taking bride | casarse; matrimonio; desposar | 女 | woman | 女 (woman / bride) | 昏 (hūn, dusk/evening wedding rites) | 11 | 左右结构 | Depicts taking a woman (女) as wife at dusk (昏), the auspicious time for ancient matrimonial rituals. | At twilight dusk (昏), the carriage arrives to welcome the bride (女) into her new home. | Al caer el crepúsculo (昏), el carruaje llega para recibir a la novia (女) en su nuevo hogar. | 55 | VHPA | ""
  姻 | yīn | marriage affinity; in-law relationship | afinidad matrimonial; lazo por matrimonio | 女 | woman | 女 (woman, forming kinship ties) | 因 (yīn, origin/basis) | 9 | 左右结构 | Phono-semantic character pairing woman (女) with cause/foundation (因), denoting family ties forged through marriage. | A woman (女) becomes the source and reason (因) uniting two completely separate families. | Una mujer (女) se convierte en el motivo y la causa (因) que entrelaza a dos familias. | 55 | VWK | ""

mnemonics_and_roots:
  composite_memory_hook_en: Taking a bride at twilight dusk (婚) establishes the lifelong family affinity (姻) of sacred marriage.
  composite_memory_hook_es: Celebrar las nupcias al crepúsculo (婚) crea el lazo de afinidad eterna (姻) en el matrimonio.
  cultural_and_cognitive_roots: Both characters bear the woman radical (女); ancient Chinese matrimony merged the bridegroom's home welcoming at dusk ('hūn') with the alliance between two lineages ('yīn'). Thus, 婚姻 represents both emotional bonding and institutional kinship.
  tone_sandhi_and_pitch_modulation: 55-55 pitch contour. Both syllables are high level 1st tones (55); maintain an even, sustained pitch without dragging.

traps_and_cognates:
  look_alikes[4]{character,pinyin,meaning_en,distinction_note}:
    昏 | hūn | dusk; faint | Lacks the left woman radical 女
    荤 | hūn | meat; pungent food | Features grass radical 艹 on top of 军
    咽 | yān / yàn | throat; swallow | Has mouth radical 口 on the left instead of 女
    烟 | yān | smoke; cigarette | Has fire radical 火 on the left instead of 女
  etymological_cognates[4]{character,pinyin,gloss_en}:
    嫁 | jià | marry off a daughter
    娶 | qǔ | marry a woman as wife
    妻 | qī | wife in the 女 radical network
    妇 | fù | married woman; matron

semantic_boundary_contrasts:
  core_nuance: 婚姻 specifically designates the formal institution, legal contract, and marital status of being husband and wife.
  contrasts[3]{id,compared_word,pinyin,analysis}:
    1 | 婚姻 vs. 婚礼 | hūnlǐ | 婚礼 is the one-time ceremonial wedding celebration or nuptial service, whereas 婚姻 refers to the ongoing institution, contract, and relationship.
    2 | 婚姻 vs. 感情 | gǎnqíng | 感情 refers to subjective emotional feelings or affection between any persons, whereas 婚姻 is a socially ratified and legalized status.
    3 | 婚姻 vs. 恋爱 | liàn'ài | 恋爱 denotes romantic courtship and dating before or without marriage, whereas 婚姻 entails civil rights and legal obligations.

extended_reading_passages[2]{id,hanzi,pinyin,en,es}:
  #1 | 美满的婚姻绝非一劳永逸的誓言，而是两个人共同构筑的避风港。当最初的激情随岁月沉淀，唯有彼此的真诚与体谅，才能在日复一日的平淡琐碎中抵御风雨，让婚姻成为灵魂深处最温暖的依靠。 | Měimǎn de hūnyīn jué fēi yíláoyǒngyì de shìyán, érshì liǎng gè rén gòngtóng gòuzhù de bìfēnggǎng. Dāng zuìchū de jīqíng suí suìyuè chéndiàn, wéiyǒu bǐcǐ de zhēnchéng yǔ tǐliàng, cáinǐng zài rìfùyírì de píngdàn suǒsuì zhōng dǐyù fēngyǔ, ràng hūnyīn chéngwéi línghún shēnchù zuì wēnnuǎn de yīkào. | A fulfilling marriage is no one-and-done vow, but a shared haven built by two people. When initial passion settles with years, only sincerity and mutual understanding weather life's storms, making marriage the warmest anchor of the soul. | Un matrimonio pleno no es un juramento estático, sino un refugio edificado entre dos. Cuando la pasión juvenil madura con los años, solo la sinceridad y la comprensión mutua resisten las tormentas, convirtiendo la unión en el ancla más cálida del alma.
  #2 | 从法理学视角审视，现代婚姻制度兼具人身伦理属性与重大财产法效力。民法典婚姻家庭编通过完善婚前财产登记与夫妻共同债务认定标准，为保护弱势配偶权益与维护交易安全提供了坚实的制度保障。 | Cóng fǎlǐxué shìjiǎo shěnshì, xiàndài hūnyīn zhìdù jiānjù rénshēn lúnlǐ shǔxìng yǔ zhòngdà cáichǎnfǎ xiàolì. Mínfǎdiǎn hūnyīn jiātíng biān tōngguò wánshàn hūnqián cáichǎn dēngjì yǔ fūqī gòngtóng zhàiwù rèndìng biāozhǔn, wèi bǎohù ruòshì pèi'ǒu quányì yǔ wéihù jiāoyì ānquán tígōng le jiānshí de zhìdù bǎozhàng. | From a legal perspective, modern marriage embodies ethical personal relations and significant property rights. The Civil Code protects vulnerable spouses and preserves transaction security through refined premarital asset registration and joint debt standards. | Desde la jurisprudencia, el matrimonio moderno conjuga lazos éticos personales con efectos patrimoniales. El Código Civil protege a los cónyuges vulnerables y garantiza la seguridad jurídica regulando el patrimonio prematrimonial y las deudas comunes.
